WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.130
Shells store carbon as calcium carbonate.

2
00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:07.690
On the seafloor, they pile up
and, in time, become limestone.

3
00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.210
In fact, most of Earth's
carbon is stored in rocks.

4
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.010
Above ground, carbon moves fast.

5
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.010
Plants draw it from the
air each northern summer;

6
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.170
decay releases it each winter.

7
00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:22.370
So how does any rock carbon
get back into the air?

8
00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.190
Or does it never escape?

9
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.590
In this mission, you'll map Earth's carbon
stores and the fast flows between air,

10
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.090
plants and soil.

11
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.430
Then you'll follow carbon
into the deep ocean,

12
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.910
and round a cycle that
runs through rock itself.

13
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.870
Your mission: find out how carbon locked
in rock finds its way back into the air.
